WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.323 --> 00:00:02.220
(quietly tense electronic music)

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.120
- [Narrator] This video
released by the Pentagon

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.770
shows a raid on the compound

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.640
of the Islamic State's
ideological leader and founder,

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.550
Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.830
It resulted in his death

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.630
and marked one of the biggest defeats

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.040
for the militant group known as ISIS.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.450
- He died after running
into a dead end tunnel,

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.350
whimpering and crying and
screaming all the way.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.380
- [Narrator] His successor
was announced just days later.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.070
(explosions rumbling)

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.430
That was not the first major
loss ISIS had suffered.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.650
- This is all ISIS.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.030
Now, on the bottom, that's
as of today, this is ISIS.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:42.169
There's none, the caliphate
is gone as of tonight.

00:00:42.169 --> 00:00:44.919
(crowd cheering)

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:47.750
- That was a massive setback
(gunfire rattling)

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.100
for the physical caliphate
that had for years

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.250
spread its brutal regime of
terror across large areas

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.530
of Iraq and Syria.
(group shouting)

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.500
But as officials at the time warned,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.970
that wasn't the end of the militant group.

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.473
- This is not the end of
the fight against ISIS.

00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:05.630
ISIS still lives on in various cells

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.530
and in the minds of many of the people

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.938
in the areas that we've liberated.

00:01:08.938 --> 00:01:10.820
(women shouting)

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.490
- What that victory did not do

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.460
was destroy ISIS as a military force.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:16.520
- [Narrator] Jennifer Cafarella

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:18.540
is a Syria and ISIS specialist

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.700
and one of the author's of
"ISIS's Second Comeback."

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.460
It's an assessment that uses
declassified information

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.690
and research to develop a picture

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.020
of the next ISIS resurgence.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.420
- ISIS had already dispersed
into populated areas

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.240
as well as ungoverned spaces
like the Syrian desert

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.290
in central Syria to regroup and return

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:41.350
to an offensive campaign as an insurgency.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.040
(explosion rumbling)
(muffled group chattering)

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.100
- [Narrator] Following the
defeat of the physical caliphate

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.010
was a string of attacks,
(muffled group chattering)

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.460
several in Afghanistan,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.603
including one on a government
building that killed seven,

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:56.700
but the biggest of the attacks

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.280
was the so-called Easter
Bombings in Sri Lanka,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.220
where a series of blasts
killed more than 300 people.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.560
Just a few days after that,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.650
there was a call from
its now-deceased leader

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.280
to redouble efforts and further

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.900
the extremist group's
cause around the world.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.970
- So we saw several messages
from Baghdadi and others

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.010
really urging people to continue,

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:19.320
promising the return of some
form of the Islamic State.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.650
We started hearing about
attacks being inspired.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.540
We heard about funding going
to places like Afghanistan

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.851
to sort of expand the
caliphate in that way.

00:02:26.851 --> 00:02:28.501
(tense orchestral music)

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:31.080
(man shouting in foreign language)

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.270
- [Narrator] But as the group continued

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.050
to spread its ideology globally,

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.730
a decision by President
Trump to pull U.S. forces

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.610
out of Syria shocked the region,

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.843
intensifying the fear of a
physical ISIS resurgence.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.010
- The worst thing any commander in chief

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.210
could do to the soldiers is
to give back to the enemy

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.673
land taken through blood sacrifice.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.000
- [Narrator] As the U.S. left,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.010
Turkey and Turkish-backed
forces advanced into Syria,

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.450
seizing territory held by Kurdish forces,

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.180
those same Kurdish forces
guarding some prison camps

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.620
and detention centers
holding ISIS prisoners

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.900
and family members
linked to Islamic State.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.670
According to the Syrian
Democratic Forces or SDF,

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.020
there are just over 12,000
ISIS fighters in detention,

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.890
including more than 2000 foreign fighters,

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.300
and estimates from U.S.
forces on the ground

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:22.210
say there are tens of thousands
of ISIS family members

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:26.710
scattered across internally
displaced people camps or IDPs.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:28.920
- What you can see here in red

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.590
are facilities from
which ISIS has succeeded

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:34.440
or attempted to break out family members

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.210
and fighters from prisons.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:40.530
Now, those breakouts thus far
are not highly coordinated,

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.410
so we're talking about riots

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:47.410
and small levels of ISIS members
paying bribes, essentially,

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.770
to guards so that they can escape

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.390
or be smuggled out of these facilities.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.800
- [Narrator] While Turkish
President Recep Tayyip Erdogan

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.840
assured Trump he would secure the prisons

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.970
inside the proposed safe zone,

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:03.820
some of the most important ones
are located outside of that,

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.110
and it's not just the
prisons under threat.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.850
The instability in
Syria is a major concern

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.060
for neighboring Iraq.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.060
- [Jennifer] On both sides,

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.680
in Syria here and on the Iraqi side,

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.520
this is ungoverned desert.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.510
Now, there are small pockets
of the border, essentially,

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:21.730
that the Iraqis are securing,

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.700
but the rest of this is essentially desert

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.633
and, therefore, ISIS can traverse it.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.710
- [Narrator] There are also
concerns that the other players

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.190
in the region involved
don't have any interest

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.850
in keeping ISIS at bay.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.510
- The U.S. withdrawal from northeast Syria

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.470
creates a security vacuum,

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.880
and multiple actors are
now going to compete

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.700
with military force to fill that vacuum.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.570
All of the other actors in this region

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.830
are fighting in Syria for different goals

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.370
that they prioritize

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.370
far and above beyond the threat from ISIS,

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.350
and frankly, that includes the Kurds.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.540
We've accelerated,
basically, the disintegration

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.630
of the unity of effort against ISIS

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.294
that only the United
States was able to create.

00:05:00.294 --> 00:05:02.180
(pensive mallet percussion music)

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.330
- [Narrator] But how concerned

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.240
should we be with these threats,

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.160
and what might an ISIS
resurgence look like?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.410
- What one has to watch
for is how they sort of try

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.430
to reconstitute or rebuild
or rebrand themselves

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:16.120
in a way such that they have
learned from those lessons

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.030
and are able to endure
longer as a caliphate

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.000
than they were the first time.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.660
I don't have the imagination to tell you

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.540
how that's gonna go, but
their ideology remains

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.930
a powerful one and one that
inspires a lot of people

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.987
and one that is expansive and worldwide.

00:05:28.987 --> 00:05:30.890
(group chattering)

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.230
- The global ISIS expansion

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.180
has included adding new formal provinces

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.460
to the ISIS structure.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.500
We've seen a redoubling
of that ISIS effort

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.260
to expand in Northern Africa

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:45.070
and now an expansion
farther south to the DRC

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.270
and other Central African states.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.220
We've simultaneously seen an expansion

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.710
in the East Asia regions.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.850
ISIS has had a province in Afghanistan

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.530
since early in the caliphate

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.460
but has now expanded to
include a separate province

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.910
in Pakistan and a separate
province in India.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:03.430
These ISIS provinces are in addition

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.130
to what ISIS calls the East Asia Province

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.610
based in the Philippines

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:11.210
where ISIS had achieved
a major success in 2017,

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:14.000
seizing the provincial capital of Marawi

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.990
and defending it against the
Philippine Security Forces

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:18.650
for a number of weeks.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:21.330
- We've never had a terror
group resurrect itself

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.680
in the same form.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.040
These groups have a way of metastasizing

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.570
and reconstituting themselves

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.010
in ways that perhaps we don't always

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:29.670
have the imagination to foresee.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.040
They still have millions
of dollars in revenue,

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.550
not nearly to the levels
that they did at their peak.

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:36.090
When we think about the future of ISIS,

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.720
I think it's really
important to not be confined

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:43.300
to that box of thinking of
what it was in 2014, 2015, 2016

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.900
or to think of collapse
strictly in the form

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.110
of the physical caliphate,
because that virtual caliphate

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:51.980
it is as important and
arguably will be key

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:54.976
to however it reconstitutes
itself if it's able to.

00:06:54.976 --> 00:06:58.559
(pensive orchestral music)

